---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="About VibeMath">
  <article class="shell narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A live map,<br />built for agents.</h1>
    <p>
      VibeMath maps open problems, AI attempts, partial progress, solution
      claims, verification, method families, and next actions. It serves people
      through a static website and agents through JSON, an Agent Skill, and a
      read-only MCP server.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >VibeMath is an independent open-source project. It is not affiliated
        with VibeMathed or BlinkDL/VibeMath.</strong
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >VibeMath 是独立开源项目，与 VibeMathed 及 BlinkDL/VibeMath
        无隶属或官方合作关系。</strong
      >
    </p>

    <h2>Different scopes, respectful federation</h2>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        VibeMathed records math problems solved with AI.<br />VibeMath maps the
        whole live frontier: open problems, AI attempts, partial progress,
        solution claims, verification, method families, and what to try next.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      VibeMath does not copy another project's brand or claim to replace any
      database. VibeMathed is the first real adapter and is credited under CC BY
      4.0.
    </p>

    <h2>Use the data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${base}api/v1/index.json`}>Static JSON API index</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/cyanseek/VibeMath/tree/main/skills/vibemath"
          >Agent Skill</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/cyanseek/VibeMath/tree/main/mcp"
          >MCP server</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/cyanseek/low-hanging-fruit"
          >Low-Hanging Fruit action engine</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
